Third-party software
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

osquery
  Version: 5.18.1
  License: Apache License 2.0 (see src-tauri/vendor/licenses/LICENSE-Apache-2.0)
  Source:  https://github.com/osquery/osquery/releases/tag/5.18.1
  KlaayGuard bundles the osquery binary as a sidecar and runs read-only
  queries against it.

Rust dependencies
  KlaayGuard links many Rust crates under permissive and weak-copyleft
  licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0, BSD, ISC, CDLA-Permissive-2.0, and the
  ISC/OpenSSL license of `ring`). The full list and license texts are in
  THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, which also ships inside the installed app.

Linux AppImage — bundled system libraries
  The Linux AppImage bundles unmodified upstream builds of WebKitGTK, GTK 3,
  GLib and related libraries under the GNU Lesser General Public License
  (LGPL) v2.1 or later. Their license texts ship inside the AppImage. Because
  they are unmodified, the corresponding source is available from your Linux
  distribution or upstream:
    WebKitGTK  https://webkitgtk.org/
    GTK        https://www.gtk.org/
    GLib       https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib
  The .deb and .rpm packages do not bundle these libraries; they declare them
  as runtime dependencies and the distribution provides them.

